# Project context

Solana + Anchor program that settles spot swaps after SP1 Groth16 verification. Off-chain circuit proves Merkle inclusion + solvency and binds a nullifier; on-chain code verifies proof, registered root, unused nullifier, then mutates zero-copy vault + SPL transfers.

## Layout

- `program/` — Anchor on-chain crate (`zk_spot_shield`), flat (not `programs/...`)
- `zk-circuit/io` — shared I/O types + Poseidon Merkle (no zkVM)
- `zk-circuit/guest` — SP1 guest; `zk-circuit/host` — prover driver
- `client/` — client helpers / later SDK
- `Anchor.toml` + root `Cargo.toml` — workspace source of truth
- `roadmap.md` — session checklist; mark `[x]` only when Exit passes
- `.github/workflows/` — unit + security CI must stay green (see `05-tests-security.mdc`)
- `further_explanations/glossary.md` — term map (owner vs payer vs authority, etc.)

## Stack pins

- Anchor `1.1.x`, Solana/Agave CLI on PATH, SP1 via `cargo prove` / `sp1up`
- Localnet: `solana config get` → localhost; wallet `~/.config/solana/id.json`

## Do not

- Do not invent nested `program/programs/...` layouts
- Do not commit keypairs, ledgers, `.so` proofs, or SP1 device caches (see `.gitignore`)
- Do not index `target/`, `.anchor/`, `test-ledger/`, or proof artifacts (see `.cursorignore`)
- Do not expand scope past the current `roadmap.md` Day unless asked
- Prefer `AccountLoader` / `zero_copy` for large hot accounts; no heap-heavy account deserialize on settle path
